      <RevenueAmt>30000</RevenueAmt>
      <Desc>This organization provided funds to Victoria Falls Wildlife Trust based in Victoria Falls, Zimbabwe for the purposes of the rescue and rehabilitation of wildlife. In cases where wildlife have been injured or orphaned due to human interference, Victoria Falls Wildlife Trust will help animals recover through veterinary or other care methods. The wildlife rehabilitation center allows care for rescued animals until they can be released back into the wild.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>88217</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>88217</GrantAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>20000</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>This organization provided funds to Victoria Falls Wildlife Trust based in Victoria Falls, Zimbabwe for wildlife research. Research plays a key role in finding sustainable solutions for long term conservation as human population growth puts a strain on environmental resources and wildlife habitats. Research projects include monitoring lions and their contact with humans and their domestic animals and finding ways to control conflict, spatial movement of elephants to avoid human conflict, rhinoceros conservation, and vulture conservation.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>21996</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>21996</GrantAmt>
        <Desc>This organization provided funds to Victoria Falls Wildlife Trust based in Victoria Falls, Zimbabwe to assist in the operation of the wildlife disease and forensics laboratory. The laboratory tests for zoonotic diseases and their spread. The laboratory also works to disrupt the illegal wildlife trade and tests wildlife samples for case work for wildlife crimes.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
